    '      <figcaption class="vh"><p id="iso-money-d">$100 moves from five investors through a ten-year fund into 49 companies and back.</p><p class="iso-live" aria-live="polite"></p></figcaption>',
    '    </figure>',
    '    <div class="mf-band">',
    '  <ol class="mf-ticks" aria-label="Steps">',
    '          <li><button type="button" data-i="0" aria-label="Step 1, Commit"><span class="mf-tn">1</span><span class="mf-tt">Commit</span></button></li>',
    '          <li><button type="button" data-i="1" aria-label="Step 2, Fees"><span class="mf-tn">2</span><span class="mf-tt">Fees</span></button></li>',
    '          <li><button type="button" data-i="2" aria-label="Step 3, Invest"><span class="mf-tn">3</span><span class="mf-tt">Invest</span></button></li>',
    '          <li><button type="button" data-i="3" aria-label="Step 4, The J-curve"><span class="mf-tn">4</span><span class="mf-tt">The J-curve</span></button></li>',
    '          <li><button type="button" data-i="4" aria-label="Step 5, The power law"><span class="mf-tn">5</span><span class="mf-tt">The power law</span></button></li>',
    '          <li><button type="button" data-i="5" aria-label="Step 6, Distributions"><span class="mf-tn">6</span><span class="mf-tt">Distributions</span></button></li>',
    '        </ol>',
    '      <div class="mf-nav"><button type="button" class="ebtn2" data-step="-1"><span class="arr arr--back" aria-hidden="true">←</span>Previous<span class="mf-w"> step</span></button><button type="button" class="ebtn" data-step="1">Next<span class="mf-w"> step</span><span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></button></div>',
    '    </div>',
    '  </div>',
    '  <div class="mf-side">',
    '    <div class="mf-steps">',
    '      <div class="mf-step" data-i="0"><p class="mf-k">Step 1 of 6</p><h4 class="mf-t">Commit</h4><p class="mf-x">Five limited partners promise $100 to a venture fund. The fund calls the money in over several years, as it finds companies.</p></div>',
    '          <div class="mf-step" data-i="1"><p class="mf-k">Step 2 of 6</p><h4 class="mf-t">Fees</h4><p class="mf-x">The managers charge about 2% of committed capital a year. Over a ten-year fund, that is about $20 of every $100, paid whether the fund wins or loses. “2 and 20” is typical, not universal.</p></div>',
    '          <div class="mf-step" data-i="2"><p class="mf-k">Step 3 of 6</p><h4 class="mf-t">Invest</h4><p class="mf-x">The remaining $80 goes into 49 companies. Most will return less than they cost.</p></div>',
    '          <div class="mf-step" data-i="3"><p class="mf-k">Step 4 of 6</p><h4 class="mf-t">The J-curve</h4><p class="mf-x">For the first four years the fund looks like it is losing money. Fees leave on day one. Exits come years later.</p></div>',
    '          <div class="mf-step" data-i="4"><p class="mf-k">Step 5 of 6</p><h4 class="mf-t">The power law</h4><p class="mf-x">Three companies pay for everything. Across just over 7,000 venture investments from 1985 to 2014, about half returned less than cost. The 6% that returned 10x or more produced about 60% of all returns.</p></div>',
    '          <div class="mf-step mf-step--out" data-i="5"><div class="mf-say"><p class="mf-k">Step 6 of 6</p><h4 class="mf-t">Distributions</h4><p class="mf-x">Companies sell or go public, and cash flows back. The managers keep 20% of the profit above the $100 the investors put in. The investors get the rest.</p></div>',
    '            <div class="mf-out" id="mfOut">',
    '              <label class="mf-lab" for="mfM"><span>Outcome: gross multiple on invested capital</span><output id="mfMo" for="mfM">2.0x</output></label>',
    '              <input class="wb-range" type="range" id="mfM" min="0.5" max="5" step="0.1" value="2">',
    '              <dl class="mf-read">',
    '                <div><dt>LP gets back</dt><dd id="mfLp">$148</dd></div>',
    '                <div><dt>LP multiple</dt><dd id="mfLx">1.48x</dd></div>',
    '                <div><dt>GP fees</dt><dd id="mfFe">$20</dd></div>',
    '                <div><dt>GP carry</dt><dd id="mfCa">$12</dd></div>',
    '              </dl>',
    '              <div class="mf-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i class="mf-fill" id="mfFill"></i><i class="mf-par"></i><span class="mf-par-l">$100</span></div>',
    '              <p class="mf-hint">At 1.25x gross, the investors get back exactly their $100. The managers keep their $20 in fees either way.</p>',
    '            </div>',
    '          </div>',
    '    </div>',
    '    <p class="vh" id="mfLive" aria-live="polite"></p>',
    '',
    '  </div>',
    '  <p class="mf-cap">Illustrative. Fees of 2% a year on committed capital for ten years, 20% carry above the return of all capital, no hurdle.</p>',
    '</div>',
    '<p class="mf-src" data-src="https://www.ben-evans.com/benedictevans/2016/4/28/winning-and-losing"><span>Sources</span>Benedict Evans, “In praise of failure,” Aug 10, 2016, on Horsley Bridge data. Fee and carry terms are illustrative.</p>',
    '<div class="wpf">',
    '  <div class="wpf-h">',
    '    <h4 class="wpf-t">Who gets paid first</h4>',
    '    <p>When a company sells, money fills the stack from the bottom. Drag the price and watch who stays dry.</p>',
    '    <p class="wpf-cap">Illustrative company. 1x non-participating preferences; preferred converts when common is worth more.</p>',
    '  </div>',
    '  <figure class="iso wpf-fig" id="csFig" data-iso="capital-stack">',
